cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Prot2Vec: a benchmark harness for protein sequence embeddings"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kunapareddy
    given-names: Sai Nikhil
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikhil-kunapareddy/Prot2Vec"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
abstract: >-
  Prot2Vec benchmarks biological sequence embedding methods on group
  separability. It compares interpretable descriptors (amino acid composition,
  dipeptide composition, physicochemical profiles, CTD), corpus-derived
  representations (k-mer TF-IDF, positional one-hot) and pretrained models
  (ESM-2, ProtBERT, ProtT5, Ankh, general-purpose LLM embedding APIs) across
  thirteen dimensionality reduction methods, scoring every pair with
  thirty-one metrics spanning projection fidelity, classification, retrieval,
  clustering agreement and confound diagnostics. Protein, DNA and RNA
  alphabets are supported, with curated Pfam seed alignments or user-supplied
  FASTA as input.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence embeddings
  - proteomics
  - protein embeddings
  - protein language models
  - representation learning
  - Pfam
  - benchmark
